{"type":"npc","name":"Calliophant","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":240,"temp":0,"max":240,"details":""},"ac":{"value":28,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"resistances":[{"type":"physical","value":10,"exceptions":["adamantine"],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":11},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Calliophants are enormous constructs that resemble brass elephants. Their hollow bodies each house a specially constructed steam organ. Magic runes convert water from an internal reservoir into steam, which passes through the organ to make music. Although calliophants lack a traditional consciousness or intelligence, they have a special processing unit for recording music, which can hold up to 24 hours' worth of music that they can later reproduce at their creator's direction.</p><p>In addition to boosting morale through their musical performances, calliophants can weaponize their musical equipment and their tremendous bulk in battle. Calliophants are extremely expensive and difficult to produce, so they are most often commissioned by city governments or nobles to serve as mobile sources of entertainment for guests at festivals and parties. Additionally, calliophants serve as excellent companions for wealthy travelers, preventing boredom and providing protection in the event of an ambush.</p><p>Calliophants left without instruction for long periods occasionally produce music that is unfamiliar to their creator. Some theorize that these tunes represent original compositions that belie the creature's traditional mindless classification. Others speculate they are reflexive tuning behaviors created by combining random parts of familiar compositions or perhaps a snippet of music that the construct detected from passersby.</p><h2>Martial Melodies</h2><p>A bygone kingdom experimented with using calliophants as beasts of war, arraying them on the front lines against an opposing army, hoping to gain a massive advantage in their presence alone. However, even before the battle began, the calliophants' discordant noises, each producing ear-splitting tunes at different tempos, caused panic in the horses of the allied cavalry and deafened soldiers, preventing them from hearing any combat orders. In the end, the calliophants' army was defeated by a crack team of enemy engineers with wax in their ears, who used drills and siphons to drain the calliophants' water reservoirs.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 175/390/720 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (heavy), shield, skill items (Athletics, Performance)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, burning barbs, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (spirit, vitality, void), fire, fire shield, music, sensory (low-light vision), strength, sturdy, water, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Ben Kobrak","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":7},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":8},"int":{"mod":-5},"wis":{"mod":0},"cha":{"mod":-5}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":17,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":20,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":24,"special":[]},"performance":{"base":21,"note":"internal steam organ only","special":[]}},"traits":{"value":["construct","mindless"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"_id":"6V6xBT4YoprzwmQe","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/calliophant.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Calliophant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"